          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>John Keats's Early Life</strong><br>\nJohn Keats was born in 1795 in London, England. He was the eldest of four children in a lower-middle-class family. After his father's death, Keats's mother remarried, but the marriage was unstable, leaving Keats to seek comfort in literature and art.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Medical Training and Literary Pursuits</strong><br>\nKeats initially trained as a surgeon, believing it to be a steady source of income while he pursued poetry. However, his medical career was short-lived as he became increasingly invested in writing poetry, a passion that would define the rest of his life.</p>\n\n<p><strong>First Published Poems</strong><br>\nKeats’s first volume of poems, published in 1817, received little attention, but he remained undeterred. His determination to become a poet was driven by a desire to make an indelible mark on the world through his verse, often exploring themes of beauty, art, and mortality.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
